WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.352
NumPy provides common descriptive statistics directly on arrays.

00:00:04.352 --> 00:00:07.682
Here we have seven daily website-visit counts.

00:00:07.682 --> 00:00:10.572
Click Run and examine the results.

00:00:10.572 --> 00:00:13.267
Sum gives us the total activity.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:16.162
Mean gives us the average daily visits.

00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:20.442
Median gives us the middle value after ordering the observations.

00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:26.947
Standard deviation gives us a measure of variability, while minimum and maximum show the observed range.

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:34.502
These summaries are useful during exploratory data analysis because they help us understand the center and

00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:37.317
spread of the data before building more complicated models.

00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:41.447
But remember that a single statistic never tells the whole story.

00:00:41.447 --> 00:00:46.457
Two datasets can have similar means but very different distributions.

00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:52.232
In real projects, use numerical summaries together with plots, domain knowledge,

00:00:52.232 --> 00:00:55.297
and checks for missing or unusual values.

00:00:55.297 --> 00:00:57.862
NumPy gives us the calculations.

00:00:57.862 --> 00:01:01.829
The analyst still has to interpret what those calculations mean.
